{"type":"text","timestamp":1788478509445,"sessionID":"ses_f96638f92ffeVKEyZreH0UcHVL","part":{"id":"prt_069a045840011JFYRrUhL9uVuj","messageID":"msg_069a03888001VdR1yUd8EP0p3b","sessionID":"ses_f96638f92ffeVKEyZreH0UcHVL","type":"text","text":"All done. Implementation complete:\n\n**`dspy/predict/react.py`**\n- Added `aforward` (dspy/predict/react.py:101) — async mirror of `forward`: same reasoning/action loop, `max_iters` support, trajectory collection (`thought_N`, `tool_name_N`, `tool_args_N`, `observation_N`), tool errors captured as observations, `finish` detection, and a final `dspy.Prediction(trajectory=..., **extract)`.\n- Added `_async_call_with_potential_trajectory_truncation` (dspy/predict/react.py:137) — awaits `module.acall(...)` and on `ContextWindowExceededError` truncates the oldest trajectory entries and retries up to 3 times.\n\n**`dspy/primitives/tool.py`**\n- `Tool.acall` (dspy/primitives/tool.py:176) now auto-detects: awaits if the result is a coroutine, otherwise returns the sync result directly instead of raising \"non-async tool\" — so sync and async tools mix freely in async workflows.\n\n**Verification**: 26 tests pass in `tests/predict/test_react.py` + `tests/primitives/test_tool.py` (including new async tests for pydantic args, error retry, and mixed sync/async tools); `ruff check`/`format` clean; the one `test_mcp.py` failure is pre-existing on the clean tree.","time":{"start":1788478506372,"end":1788478509442}}}
